Updated implementation snapshot (2026-09-24)
- Express/Prisma API runs from src/index.js on PORT or 6000, with /health public and /api protected by optional x-api-key authentication.
- Current routes include the CRUD resources below plus /api/audit-logs, /api/ai, and /api/voice-assistant. The older standalone speech/analyze paths are no longer mounted by app.js.
- The AI agent uses Gemini fallback models, bounded conversation history, a five-iteration tool loop, and tools for data operations and UI navigation.
- Voice processing accepts multipart audio with multer, transcribes Arabic through Groq Whisper, analyzes text, and stores transcription/analysis JSON files under uploads/ and results/.
- The API uses generic pagination/CRUD helpers, UUID and body validation, Prisma transactions for property relation updates, and standard { data, pagination } responses.
- Required DATABASE_URL and GEMINI_API_KEY; optional PORT, FRONTEND_URL, API_KEY, GROQ_API_KEY, and other AI/audio settings.

